abstract: >-
  An evidence-driven Quality Engineering framework for performance and
  reliability testing of AI applications and AI agents. The work covers
  realistic AI workload modeling, SLOs, percentile latency, TTFT, TPOT,
  end-to-end task latency, throughput, context growth, RAG and agentic
  trajectories, tokens and cost per successful task, concurrency, queueing,
  fault injection, timeouts, retries, idempotency, fallback, recovery,
  observability, baseline regression, CI/CD quality gates and safe capacity
  testing.